\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Annual NOAA-Reported Financial Damage for High-Confidence Matched Flood Events: Shows how total NOAA-reported financial damage varies over time, with a small number of years accounting for much of the observed loss.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Number of High-Confidence Matched NOAA Flood Events by Year: Shows how the number of corroborated flash-flood events changes over time and provides context for interpreting annual damage totals.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Annual Matched Flood Frequency vs Maximum NOAA-Reported Event Damage: Compares annual matched-event frequency with the largest individual NOAA-reported loss in each year. The relationship shows that years with more floods do not necessarily contain more severe individual events and that annual losses can be dominated by a single extreme flood.\
